  "mergedAt": "2026-05-19T17:45:24Z",
  "title": "Replace Blazor WebAssembly DevServer with Gateway in templates",
  "updatedAt": "2026-05-19T17:46:16Z",
  "retrievedAtUtc": "2026-10-31T16:31:54.5245560Z",
  "body": "## Summary\n\nThis PR replaces the Blazor WebAssembly DevServer with the Blazor Gateway in the standalone WASM template, and leverages the SDK's built-in `StaticWebAssetSpaFallbackEnabled` property instead of the custom `SpaFallback.targets`.\n\n## Changes\n\n### Commit 1: Remove ThreadingApp and multi-threading testing support\nMulti-threading is not currently supported. Removes ThreadingApp, ThreadingApp.Server, associated test files, and the multi-threading helper infrastructure.\n\n### Commit 2: Use SDK StaticWebAssetSpaFallbackEnabled instead of custom SpaFallback.targets\n- Deletes `src/Components/WebAssembly/testassets/SpaFallback.targets`\n- Adds `StaticWebAssetSpaFallbackEnabled=true` to StandaloneApp and the benchmark TestApp\n- The SDK now generates `{**fallback:nonfile}` endpoints in the manifest at build time\n\n### Commit 3: Remove MapFallbackToFile from BlazorGateway\nSince the SPA fallback is now handled via the static web assets endpoints manifest (served by `MapStaticAssets`), the Gateway no longer needs to call `MapFallbackToFile`.\n\n### Commit 4: Update WASM template to use Blazor Gateway instead of DevServer\n- Replaces `Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.DevServer` with `Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Gateway`\n- Adds `OverrideHtmlAssetPlaceholders` and `StaticWebAssetSpaFallbackEnabled` properties\n\n## Dependencies\n\nRequires SDK fix: https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/pull/54353\n\n## Testing\n\n- Built repo successfully\n- Verified StandaloneApp E2E with Gateway + SPA fallback\n- Verified instantiated blazorwasm template E2E with patched SDK\r\n"
}
